# Build context for packages/whatsapp-bot/Dockerfile (#236), which is built from the REPO
# ROOT. A WHITELIST: everything is excluded, then exactly what the bot image needs is let
# back in — the workspace manifests (pnpm resolves the graph from them), the shared
# package's sources (inlined into the bundle), and the bot's own sources, groups and
# scripts. Never the embeddings, the puzzle stores, node_modules or cdk.out.
#
# **NO WILDCARD IN THE MIDDLE OF A RE-INCLUDE.** A directory excluded by `*` is walked only
# when some `!` pattern LITERALLY starts with that directory's path — the check is a string
# prefix, not a match. So `!packages/*/package.json` never rescues `packages/generation/`:
# the walk skips the whole directory and the manifest disappears, and `pnpm install
# --frozen-lockfile` then fails because the lockfile names an importer the context does not
# have. Every path below therefore names its directories outright, which is also why ADDING
# A WORKSPACE PACKAGE means adding a line here (the same duty as wiring it into deploy.yml).
#
# The CDK asset fingerprint honours this file too, so only these paths trigger a rebuild.
*

# The workspace itself. `tsconfig.base.json` is what every package's tsconfig extends;
# without it esbuild warns on each build and silently falls back on its own defaults.
!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!tsconfig.base.json

# Every member's manifest: a frozen install validates the lockfile against all of them.
!packages/backend/package.json
!packages/benchmark/package.json
!packages/curation/package.json
!packages/generation/package.json
!packages/infra/package.json
!packages/shared/package.json
!packages/web/package.json
!packages/whatsapp-bot/package.json

# What the image actually compiles and runs.
!packages/shared/src
!packages/shared/tsconfig.json
!packages/whatsapp-bot/Dockerfile
!packages/whatsapp-bot/groups
!packages/whatsapp-bot/scripts
!packages/whatsapp-bot/src
!packages/whatsapp-bot/tsconfig.json

# Last word, so nothing above can drag these in.
**/node_modules
**/dist
